        "In older adults or individuals dealing with chronic systemic inflammation, a condition known as anabolic resistance blunts the sensitivity of Sestrin2 and mTORC1 signaling. Older lifters frequently require 3.5 to 4.2 grams of leucine per meal to initiate the identical ribosomal phosphorylation cascade that a twenty-year-old athlete achieves with only 2.0 grams. Overcoming anabolic resistance necessitates selecting protein sources with exceptionally high biological value or supplementing meals with free-form branched-chain amino acids to ensure every feeding achieves full myofibrillar stimulation.",
